rce builds. Two are not: arc and VI came from  the old NONFREE directory, where they had been recorded as SDK  binaries in error. Both are third-party programs that happen to  arrive under a name already taken -- VI is a PVIC build, a  sibling of vi_nocio.  arc            ARC v5.12, third-party; /dd/CMDS/arc is a later build  VI             PVIC, public domain Portable VI Clone *basename.cio   archived build, needs cio; superseded by the gcc2 rebuild *cat.cio        archived build, needs cio; superseded by the gcc2 rebuild  compress       our source build; the disk already had compress *dirname.cio    archived build, needs cio; superseded by the gcc2 rebuild  kermit         our source build; CMDS/kermit is the restored C-Kermit 5A(188)  screen         our source build; CMDS/screen is the restored archive binary *strings.cio    archived build, needs cio; superseded by the gcc2 rebuild *wc.cio         archived build, needs cio; superseded by the gcc2 rebuild